    questions: [
      { question: { en: "What is the bloodline, and why is it typically trimmed away?" }, answers: ["A seasoning applied after cooking, trimmed for texture", "A dark strip of tissue from old blood vessels that can carry a strong flavor and disrupt visual tone", "A type of scale left over from an earlier step", "A bone fragment left after filleting"], correctIndex: 1, explanation: { en: "The bloodline is a dark reddish strip of tissue that can carry a stronger, sometimes metallic flavor and visually interrupts the fillet's even color." } },
      { question: { en: "How is sinew typically identified during trimming?" }, answers: ["By its bright color contrasting with the flesh", "By feel, as a firmer, resistant band running through otherwise soft flesh", "By smell alone", "It cannot be identified and is left in place"], correctIndex: 1, explanation: { en: "Sinew is identified largely by feel as a firmer, resistant band that would otherwise create an unpleasant texture if left in the flesh." } },
      { question: { en: "According to the lesson, why is presentation given as much weight as taste in traditional sushi service?" }, answers: ["Presentation is purely a modern marketing trend with no traditional basis", "Clean, even edges and consistent color signal the same level of care to a diner as balanced flavor does", "Taste is considered less important than appearance in professional kitchens", "Presentation only matters for fish that will be photographed"], correctIndex: 1, explanation: { en: "In traditional sushi service, visual presentation carries weight comparable to taste, since clean trimming signals the same level of care as good flavor." } },
      { question: { en: "What is the recommended approach to removing a bloodline efficiently?" }, answers: ["Many short, choppy cuts across the strip", "A single continuous strip removal to avoid wasting surrounding flesh", "Scraping it off with the back of the knife", "Leaving it in place and covering it with sauce"], correctIndex: 1, explanation: { en: "Removing the bloodline as one continuous strip wastes far less surrounding flesh than several overlapping small cuts." } },
    ],
